 "thread": "aafekEb26yE",
 "subject": "Looking for details of spectral approximation when using non-integer alpha",
 "messages_listed": 3,
 "last_activity": "2020-06-16T07:36:39Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "QmBlAzmDBAAJ",
   "from": "Mark",
   "author": "a51b9d9ec6729a87",
   "date": "2020-06-16T04:11:29Z",
   "subject": "Looking for details of spectral approximation when using non-integer alpha",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font color=\"#000000\">Hello everyone,</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><font color=\"#000000\">From Bakka et al </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> (Spatial modeling with R-INLA: A review, 2018)</span><font color=\"#000000\">:</font><div><font color=\"#000000\">&quot;...a restriction with the SPDE approach is that it is only computable if α is an integer...&quot;</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">From INLA documentation </font><i style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);box-sizing:inherit;font-family:Lato,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">(</i><a href=\"https://rdrr.io/github/andrewzm/INLA/man/inla.spde2.matern.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rdrr.io/github/andrewzm/INLA/man/inla.spde2.matern.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440707963000&amp;usg=AOvVaw23z8Q9XwKj3uugl8NwOEX7\">https://rdrr.io/github/andrewzm/INLA/man/inla.spde2.matern.html</a><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">:</span></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Lato,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Stationary models are supported for </span><i style=\"box-sizing:inherit;font-family:Lato,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">0 &lt; α ≤q 2</i><span style=\"font-family:Lato,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">, with spectral approximation methods used for non-integer </span><i style=\"box-sizing:inherit;font-family:Lato,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">α&quot;</i></font></div><div><br></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">Where can I learn about how the <font face=\"Lato, Helvetica Neue, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">spectral approximation method is used in the context of INLA?</span></font></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Lato, Helvetica Neue, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br></span></font></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Lato, Helvetica Neue, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Basically, I fit a bunch of models and half of them use alpha=3/2, so I&#39;m wondering what I built the mesh for!)</span></font></font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Lato,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></div><div><font face=\"Lato, Helvetica Neue, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Best,</span></font></div><div><font face=\"Lato, Helvetica Neue, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"Lato, Helvetica Neue, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mark</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "FYHGIl9aBwAJ",
   "from": "Finn Lindgren",
   "author": "afb003e064114795",
   "date": "2020-06-16T06:51:24Z",
   "subject": "Re: [r-inla] Looking for details of spectral approximation when using non-integer alpha",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\">Hi,<div>The sentence in the review paper is a bit unclear. It should really say that the “basic” construction of the SPDE/GMRF representation works for integer alpha, but that further techniques can yield GMRF approximations also for non-integer alpha.</div><div>The current implementation for fractional alpha values is based on the spectral approximation technique discussed in the Authors’ Response in the Discussion of the Lindgren, Rue, Lindström 2011 JRSSB paper (see references in the review paper).<br><br><div dir=\"ltr\">Finn</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><blockquote type=\"cite\">On 16 Jun 2020, at 05:11, Mark &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mille...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br><br></blockquote></div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\">﻿</div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font color=\"#000000\">Hello everyone,</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><font color=\"#000000\">From Bakka et al </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> (Spatial modeling with R-INLA: A review, 2018)</span><font color=\"#000000\">:</font><div><font color=\"#000000\">&quot;...a restriction with the SPDE approach is that it is only computable if α is an integer...&quot;</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">From INLA documentation </font><i style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);box-sizing:inherit;font-family:Lato,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">(</i><a href=\"https://rdrr.io/github/andrewzm/INLA/man/inla.spde2.matern.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rdrr.io/github/andrewzm/INLA/man/inla.spde2.matern.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440707965000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1eO2g_sDBVcIb7fDVZKCdP\">https://rdrr.io/github/andrewzm/INLA/man/inla.spde2.matern.html</a><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">:</span></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Lato,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Stationary models are supported for </span><i style=\"box-sizing:inherit;font-family:Lato,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">0 &lt; α ≤q 2</i><span style=\"font-family:Lato,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">, with spectral approximation methods used for non-integer </span><i style=\"box-sizing:inherit;font-family:Lato,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">α&quot;</i></font></div><div><br></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">Where can I learn about how the <font face=\"Lato, Helvetica Neue, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">spectral approximation method is used in the context of INLA?</span></font></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Lato, Helvetica Neue, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br></span></font></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Lato, Helvetica Neue, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Basically, I fit a bunch of models and half of them use alpha=3/2, so I&#39;m wondering what I built the mesh for!)</span></font></font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Lato,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></div><div><font face=\"Lato, Helvetica Neue, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Best,</span></font></div><div><font face=\"Lato, Helvetica Neue, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"Lato, Helvetica Neue, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mark</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><br></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></div></blockquote></div></div>"
